Stable client endpoint ID.
@opt **--relay-mode** *mode*
@cli values: untrusted trusted
@cli spell: --relay-mode <mode>
@cli help: untrusted or trusted

Relay trust mode: **untrusted** or **trusted**.
@opt **--relay-trust-mode** *mode*
@cli values: tofu pinned
@cli spell: --relay-trust-mode <mode>
@cli help: tofu (default) or pinned
@cli column: 28

End-to-end relay-v2 peer identity policy. The default **tofu** records the
first identity only after a successful authenticated ordinary-channel
handshake. The **pinned** mode refuses peers without an explicit pin. Neither
mode permits identity replacement.
@opt **--relay-trust-dir** *path*
@cli file: yes
@cli spell: --relay-trust-dir <path>
@cli help: Owner-only relay-v2 peer identity store

Owner-only relay-v2 peer identity store. Entries are bound to the exact
endpoint ID and are opened without following links.
@opt **--relay-peer-pin** *endpoint=64hex*
@cli spell: --relay-peer-pin <id=64hex>
@cli help: Explicit composite identity pin; repeatable.
@cli help: Required for admin channels in both modes.

Configure an explicit composite-identity SHA-256 pin. This option is
repeatable. Admin channels require an explicit matching pin even when ordinary
channels use TOFU.
@opt **--allow-inbound-admin, --deny-inbound-admin**
