## RUNTIME OPTIONS

@options
@opt **--tunnels** *n*
@cli spell: --tunnels <n>
@cli help: Parallel TLS tunnels to the server (1..16; default 1;
@cli help: values above 1 require bulk-key session policy,
@cli help: or N-1 distinct --secondary-auth identities)

Open 1 to 16 parallel TLS tunnels. Counts above one require either a bulk-key
session policy or one distinct **--secondary-auth** identity for every
secondary tunnel.
@opt **--instance** *name*
@cli spell: --instance <name>
@cli help: Runtime instance name

Runtime instance name.
@opt **--history-dir** *path*
@cli spell: --history-dir <path>
@cli help: Chat history directory

Chat history directory.
@opt **--relay-receive-dir** *path*
@cli file: yes
@cli spell: --relay-receive-dir <path>
@cli help: Confined file/byte receive directory

Directory for received relay file/byte transfers. Files are created exclusively
with mode 0600 and never overwrite or follow an existing entry.
@opt **--no-history**
@cli spell: --no-history
@cli help: Disable chat history

Disable chat history.
@opt **--non-interactive**
@cli spell: --non-interactive
@cli help: Disable live status redraw

Disable live status redraw.
@opt **--live-status**
@cli spell: --live-status
@cli help: Enable live status redraw

Enable live status redraw.
@opt **--timing**
@cli spell: --timing
@cli help: Emit precise timing diagnostics (developer build only)

Emit precise timing diagnostics in a Debug or RelWithDebInfo developer build.
Release and MinSizeRel binaries compile these hooks out and warn that the
option is unavailable.
@opt **--boring**
@cli spell: --boring
@cli help: Minimal output

Use minimal output.
@opt **--accept-server-control** *[port]*
@cli spell: --accept-server-control [port]
@cli help: Allow the server to open a bounded reverse SSH listener

Opt in to server-initiated bounded TCP stream opens. The client publishes a
reverse listener for **127.0.0.1:22** and the server picks its own listen port
automatically. An explicit *port* pins the server-side listener and must be
**3000**-**30000**. Command execution is not part of this contract.
@opt **--accept-server-control-min-port** *port***, --accept-server-control-max-port** *port*
@cli spell: --accept-server-control-min-port <port>
@cli spell: --accept-server-control-max-port <port>
@cli help: Bound automatic reverse-listener selection

Bound the automatically chosen server-side listener range used when no explicit
**--accept-server-control** port is pinned. The default range is
**4100**-**8600**. Positive values are clamped to 1-65535; a non-positive value
keeps that side's default. An inverted pair is swapped. Passing either option
also enables **--accept-server-control**.
@opt **--service-streams-only**
@cli spell: --service-streams-only
@cli help: Embedder mode: keep only ABI service streams

Embedder mode: keep only the ABI service streams. The session stays up without
a local-attach runtime, an interactive console, or any listener of its own.
@opt **--**
@cli spell: --
@cli help: Service-safe launch
@cli column: 28

Service-safe launch separator.
@end

